@startuml
title MODFLOW 6 To Simulated Active Network
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam wrapWidth 180
skinparam maxMessageSize 180

actor User
participant "hydromodpy run" as Run
participant "MODFLOW 6 GWF" as MF6
participant "Modflow6OutputAdapter" as Adapter
database "SimulationCatalog\nZarr + DuckDB" as Catalog
participant "Derived extractor" as Derived
participant "Run API" as RunApi
participant "Display layer" as Display

User -> Run : run simulation TOML
Run -> MF6 : write packages and execute
MF6 --> Adapter : heads (.hds)\nbudgets (.cbc)\ngrid binary (.grb)

Adapter -> Catalog : write head and budget fields
Adapter -> Catalog : write mesh/vertices\nmesh/face_node_connectivity\nmesh/surface_top

Derived -> Catalog : read raw DRN budget
Derived -> Catalog : write derived/outflow_drain\npositive, layer-summed
Derived -> Catalog : write derived/accumulation_flux\nD8 route, mesh route, or fallback

User -> RunApi : run.fields("accumulation_flux")
RunApi -> Catalog : read solver field
Catalog --> RunApi : reshape on solver support\nwhen structured_shape is known

User -> Display : run.plot("simulated_active_network")
Display -> RunApi : simulated_active_network_mask(...)
Display -> Catalog : read accumulation_flux + mesh topology
Display --> User : active-network figure

note over Adapter,Catalog
The mesh topology is what allows
MODFLOW 6 results to be plotted on
the solver support rather than on
the source DEM grid.
end note

note over Derived
Raw MODFLOW drain outflow usually has
a negative budget sign. HydroModPy
stores positive outflow for result use.
end note
@enduml
